ment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 9.6% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.29 (orders outpacing sales), a backlog worth 3.3x annual revenue and deferred revenue up 3%.","Capex runs 1.6x depreciation (2.6% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 34, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.6%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only bought over the past year (2 purchases, net $317K bought).","It returns 4.9% a year to shareholders (3.5% in buybacks and 1.4% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 1.2% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 34 consecutive years, raising it 5.0% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 7,300 employees, each generates about $349K of revenue, in line with the Technology median, and revenue has grown 6.7% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $95K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.0M (6x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $4K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":90,"head":"Invest: trades 30% below fair value of $254; ROIC 22.0% vs WACC 8.0%.","pros":["Composite 60, above the 57 line (gates 18/25)","Trades 30% below fair value of $254","ROIC 22.0% vs WACC 8.0%","FCF margin 27.3%","Revenue grew 7.7%/yr over 5y"],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":216.25,"vc":{"base":254.42,"base_src":"dcf","bear":199.09,"bull":339.81,"alt_median":78.44,"n_alt":3,"gap":2.2433,"dispersion":0.4215,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (42% dispersion)","DCF is 224% above the other models' median ($78.44)"]},"med":{"pe":27.4092,"ev_ebitda":17.107,"pfcf":26.1394,"pb":3.84